<!--
    Objective-C metadata of a dyld shared cache image.

    Issue: an image rebuilt out of a cache carried classes but no methods: a
    cache's small method lists hold their selectors (`0x40000000`) and type
    strings (`0x20000000`) as offsets from the cache's selector base, the
    strings themselves live in libobjc's `__OBJC_RO` region outside the image,
    and `class_ro_t.baseMethods` with its low bit set is a relative
    list-of-lists. On Foundation out of an iOS 17 cache the `objc` pass added
    no name and typed no `self`.

    Fix: `loader/kuna_dyldcache.rs` finds the selector base in the cache
    header's ObjCOptimizationHeader (dyld 1042+), else in libobjc's
    `objc_opt_t` (`__objc_opt_ro`, version 16, +0x28); `MachoImage::with_cache`
    reads outside the image through the cache; `methods.rs` decodes the two
    flags; `classt.rs` walks the list-of-lists.

    `dyld_cache_objc.py` builds two caches with one stripped `libgreeter.dylib`
    (no symbols at all) and a `libobjc.A.dylib` owning the strings: the first
    with the ObjCOptimizationHeader, the `_v16` one without it (its header
    ends before `objcOptsOffset`), so the fallback is what finds the base.

    Pass 1 (`objc off`): the IMP is `sub_180001800`. Pass 2 and 3 (`objc on`,
    each cache): `int -[Greeter greet:](Greeter *self,objc_selector *_cmd,int arg1)`
    from the relative type string `i24@0:8i16`, and `-[Greeter count]`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
